            <ArticleTitle>Abnormal brachial artery flow-mediated vasodilation in young adults with major depression.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>196-8, A7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Depressive illness in patients without traditional risk factors for coronary artery disease is associated with striking abnormalities of endothelial function and elevation of circulating markers of atherosclerosis propensity. Further studies are needed to define the mechanisms that underlie these observations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
